=== Text #1 ===
> This magnificent compilation of play from the 1960[s] through to the 1970s forms the basis of the third part of Garry Kasparov's long-awaited definitive history[ of the World] Chess Championship. This volume features the play[ of champions] Tigran Petrosian ([1963]-1969) and[ Boris] Spassky (1969-1972).
Garry Kasparov, the thirteenth[ world] champion and widely acclaimed[ as] the[ greatest] player ever, assess[es] the contribution[ of] his 12 great predecessors. This is the second part of a three-volume series.
The history[ of] sport has seen many gladiatorial clashes: Ali v Frazier in boxing, McEnroe v Borg[ in] tennis, Prost v Senna in motor racing. This title analyses the clashes from 1984 and[ 1985],[ giving] author's opinions both on the political machinations surrounding the matches as well as the games.
In Checkmate! readers are invited to learn chess with Garry Kasparov, the[ World] number[ one] and the most[ famous] figure[ in] chess history, as their teacher. In this book chess players can discover all the various pieces and[ how they] move,[ how to] attack and[ how] to defend,[ how to] capture, and, crucially, how to give[ check] and deliver[ check]mate.
"A modern history of the early development[ of] chess."
